To utilize Java programming language to blend different audio files and create a realistic experience of a summer day, you can use a library called AudioSystem in Java. This library allows you to play and manipulate audio files.
Here's an example of how you can use AudioSystem to play multiple audio files:
```java
import java.io.File;
import javax.sound.sampled.AudioInputStream;
import javax.sound.sampled.AudioSystem;
import javax.sound.sampled.Clip;
public class AudioPlayer {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Load the first audio file
        File file1 = new File("audio1.wav");
        AudioInputStream stream1 = AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(file1);

        // Load the second audio file
        File file2 = new File("audio2.wav");
        AudioInputStream stream2 = AudioSystem.getAudioInputStream(file2);

        // Create a clip for each audio file
        Clip clip1 = AudioSystem.getClip();
        clip1.open(stream1);
        Clip clip2 = AudioSystem.getClip();
        clip2.open(stream2);

        // Play both audio files simultaneously
        clip1.start();
        clip2.start();

        // Wait until the clips have finished playing
        while (clip1.isRunning() || clip2.isRunning()) {
            Thread.sleep(100);
        }

        // Close the clips when they have finished playing
        clip1.close();
        clip2.close();
    }
}
```
This code will play two audio files simultaneously on separate channels.
